WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.608
Welcome. This is From Sounds to Words, a ten-day blending practice plan.

2
00:00:05.058 --> 00:00:09.303
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

3
00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:16.385
This plan is for a child who knows most of the letter sounds, but cannot yet push them together into a word.

4
00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:19.544
They say each sound, and then the word does not come.

5
00:00:19.994 --> 00:00:22.033
Or they look at the first letter, and guess.

6
00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:28.036
The missing skill is called blending. It is taught in small steps, and this plan is those steps.

7
00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:33.340
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

8
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:40.919
Day one is a short check that finds the reason your child is not blending yet. Day ten shows you what changed.

9
00:00:41.369 --> 00:00:47.636
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do, and how the sounds should sound.

10
00:00:48.086 --> 00:00:55.392
And every word in the plan uses only twelve sounds. Your child can sound out every word. Nothing has to be guessed.

11
00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:58.716
Here are the twelve sounds, the way they should sound.

12
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:05.832
As in nest.

13
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.187
As in moon.

14
00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:17.977
Keep every sound short and clean. Do not add an extra sound on the end.

15
00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:26.011
Now, what to expect. The plan starts with listening, with no letters at all. Then words with two sounds. Then three.

16
00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:34.629
Some days will be easy. Some will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind. It is how blending is learned.

17
00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:40.979
This plan is practice in the right order. It is not a promise. Children get there at different speeds.

18
00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:46.703
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps. So you always know what to do next.

19
00:01:47.503 --> 00:01:53.990
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

20
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:59.009
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

21
00:01:59.459 --> 00:02:02.606
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

22
00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:09.447
Then your child does the rest alone, and calls you at the end. Praise the trying, not only the right answers.

23
00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:13.734
If a page is ending in tears, put it away and do it again tomorrow.

24
00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:19.306
You need the printed pages, a pencil, some crayons, and ten quiet minutes a day.

25
00:02:19.756 --> 00:02:21.758
Keep your phone nearby, for the videos.

26
00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:27.521
You do not need any teaching training. The pages and the videos tell you exactly what to do.

27
00:02:28.321 --> 00:02:33.533
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about three minutes.
